body:
This mode has as goal to flatten the URL structure to avoid the indexName of the root index in the URL when there's only one URL.

Usage:

```js
import { history } from 'instantsearch.js/lib/router';
import { singleIndex } from 'instantsearch.js/lib/stateMappings';

instantsearch({
  // ...
  indexName: "blabla",
  routing: {
    router: history(),
    stateMapping: singleIndex("blabla"),
  },
});
```

Right now it's not yet possible to use this router in TS because InstantSearch itself isn't generic, and trying to make this happen was causing me a cascade of Generic issues. For now you need to cast it (`stateMapping: singleIndex("blabla") as StateMapping<UiState>`).

BREAKING CHANGE: Default URLs have changed, and now will contain the full state, which includes the index name. You can use the old behaviour by using the `singleIndex` stateMapping, and passing the index to synchronise in the argument.

